{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns a "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" slice, fetches a JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a so reads are synchronous and offline-capable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three flag types from one wire format:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"boolean","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — on\/off with rollout percentage (0–100)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"variant","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — string-typed weighted variants for A\/B tests."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"value","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — typed remote-tunable scalar ("},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For end-to-end wiring, see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","text":"Library target","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Wire-format","text":"Wire format","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["{","  \"version\": 1,","  \"flags\": {","    \"new_onboarding\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"rollout\": 25 },","    \"checkout_layout\": {","      \"type\": \"variant\",","      \"variants\": [","        { \"value\": \"control\", \"weight\": 50 },","        { \"value\": \"treatment\", \"weight\": 50 }","      ]","    },","    \"max_free_uploads\": { \"type\": \"value\", \"value\": 5 }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin rejects unknown "},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values and falls back to the last-known-good cache. Defaults always live in Swift at the call site — this keeps them type-checked and forces “what if missing?” thinking."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Bucketing-and-identity","text":"Bucketing and identity","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"bucket = FNV1a(bucketingID + \":\" + flagKey) % 100","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Stable per ","type":"text"},{"code":"(bucketingID, flagKey)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair forever.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Same input always produces the same bucket."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Per-flag.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A user isn’t always in the “early” group across different flags."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Identity resolution.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" When a "},{"code":"userIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is configured "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the current user ID is non-nil, that is used. Otherwise the install ID is used. Anonymous users get a stable per-install identity; logged-in users get stable cross-device assignment. A user’s variant "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"can","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" shift once at login — acceptable for nearly all real use cases."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FNV-1a was chosen because it’s simple, dependency-free, and matches GrowthBook’s algorithm so apps migrating from GrowthBook get compatible buckets."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Evaluation-order","text":"Evaluation order","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For each read, in priority:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Local override present?","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Return it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Flag in remote config?","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Evaluate (rollout \/ variant assignment \/ value lookup)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Otherwise","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" return the Swift-side default."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Persistence","text":"Persistence","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Install ID","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" persisted to "},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on first generation. Read at hydration via "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState.hydrated(from:defaultConfig:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Last-known config","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" persisted after every successful refresh. Hydrates as fallback before first network success."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Local overrides","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" persisted by default. Restart = clean state."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"exposedKeys","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" persisted. New session = fresh exposure events."}]}]}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Exposure-tracking","type":"heading","text":"Exposure tracking"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A\/B testing is only analytically valid if you know which users actually saw each variant — bucketing alone is insufficient because the code path branching on the flag might never execute."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["store.send(.featureFlags(.recordExposure(key: \"checkout_layout\")))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or via the SwiftUI sugar:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["WizardView()","    .recordsExposure(of: .checkoutLayout, store: store, action: AppAction.featureFlags)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin dedupes per session and fires the optional "},{"code":"onExposure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" callback (passed at plugin init). Wire that callback to your analytics plugin to forward exposures as events."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Refresh policy","level":2,"anchor":"Refresh-policy"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum RefreshPolicy: Sendable {","    case manual                                      \/\/ every .refresh fetches","    case automatic(minInterval: TimeInterval)        \/\/ debounce; default 300s","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps dispatch "},{"code":".refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"code":"App.scenePhase","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" transitions; the plugin’s debouncing makes this safe to call frequently. The plugin does not subscribe to "},{"code":"UIApplication","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" notifications — wiring stays in the host app."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Service protocol","level":2,"anchor":"Service-protocol"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public protocol FeatureFlagsService: Sendable {","    func fetch() async throws -> FeatureFlagsConfig","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One method. Caching, hydration, evaluation all live in the plugin."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Built-in-HTTPFeatureFlagsService","text":"Built-in: `HTTPFeatureFlagsService`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSONDecoder"},{"type":"text","text":". Apps host their JSON anywhere — static file on a CDN, Cloudflare Worker, their own server. Zero backend infrastructure required. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/"},{"type":"text","text":" is a runnable shared Worker serving flags + killswitch for a whole portfolio from one URL ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET \/<appID>\/flags"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Third-party adapters (LaunchDarkly, GrowthBook, Statsig) conform to the same protocol without changing the plugin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Typed-flag-keys","text":"Typed flag keys"},{"code":["public struct BoolFlag: Sendable, Hashable","public struct VariantFlag<Variant: RawRepresentable & Sendable> where Variant.RawValue == String","public struct ValueFlag<Value: Sendable>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read API on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["state.isEnabled(.newOnboarding, default: false)","state.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","state.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reads are pure synchronous functions. Per-property observation works as it does for any other state slice — views re-render only when the flag they read changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Action-semantics-selected","text":"Action semantics (selected)"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded(FeatureFlagsConfig, fetchedAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is dispatched on every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" (including debounced refreshes that return an unchanged config). Consume config transitions by observing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"type":"text","text":" or a value derived from it — not by mapping this action. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed featur